"},{"letter":"B","text":"Intramuscular administration"},{"letter":"C","text":"Intra-arterial administration"},{"letter":"D","text":"Subcutaneous administration"}],"multi":null,"correctSet":[],"answerIdx":null,"answerLetter":null,"answerText":null,"explanation":null},{"n":60,"chapter":"Pharmacology","src":"Loksewa paper p. 5 (Medical Officer 2083-01-04)","pdfPage":5,"stem":"A 60 year old man with a history of heart failure and reduced ejection fraction is started on a drug to improve his symptoms. The drug inhibits the sodium-potassium ATPase pump, leading to increased intracellular calcium. Which of the following drugs was most likely prescribed?","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"Digoxin"},{"letter":"B","text":"Furosemide"},{"letter":"C","text":"Lisinopril"},{"letter":"D","text":"Spironolactone"}],"multi":null,"correctSet":[],"answerIdx":null,"answerLetter":null,"answerText":null,"explanation":null},{"n":61,"chapter":"Dermatology","src":"Loksewa paper p. 5 (Medical Officer 2083-01-04)","pdfPage":5,"stem":"Which layer of the epidermis contains melanocytes?","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"Stratum basale"},{"letter":"B","text":"Stratum lucidum"},{"letter":"C","text":"Stratum spinosum"},{"letter":"D","text":"Stratum granulosum"}],"multi":null,"correctSet":[],"answerIdx":null,"answerLetter":null,"answerText":null,"explanation":null},{"n":62,"chapter":"Dermatology","src":"Loksewa paper p. 6 (Medical Officer 2083-01-04)","pdfPage":6,"stem":"All are the treatment of moderate to severe acne vulgaris EXCEPT:","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"Isotretinoin (13-cis-retinoic acid)"},{"letter":"B","text":"Calcipotriol"},{"letter":"C","text":"Carbon dioxide laser, microdermabrasion"},{"letter":"D","text":"UVB phototherapy or PDT"}],"multi":null,"correctSet":[],"answerIdx":null,"answerLetter":null,"answerText":null,"explanation":null},{"n":63,"chapter":"Medicine","src":"Loksewa paper p. 6 (Medical Officer 2083-01-04)","pdfPage":6,"stem":"What is the treatment of opportunistic infection in the case of AIDS?","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"Standard antiviral treatment"},{"letter":"B","text":"Broad spectrum antibiotics"},{"letter":"C","text":"Systemic steroid"},{"letter":"D","text":"Cotrimoxazole"}],"multi":null,"correctSet":[],"answerIdx":null,"answerLetter":null,"answerText":null,"explanation":null},{"n":64,"chapter":"Dermatology","src":"Loksewa paper p. 6 (Medical Officer 2083-01-04)","pdfPage":6,"stem":"Most common cause of Non-Gonococcal Urethritis (NGU) is:","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"Virus"},{"letter":"B","text":"Chlamydia trachomatis"},{"letter":"C","text":"Trichomonas vaginalis"},{"letter":"D","text":"Fungus"}],"multi":null,"correctSet":[],"answerIdx":null,"answerLetter":null,"answerText":null,"explanation":null},{"n":65,"chapter":"Dermatology","src":"Loksewa paper p. 6 (Medical Officer 2083-01-04)","pdfPage":6,"stem":"What is the most common site for atopic dermatitis in adults?","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"Face"},{"letter":"B","text":"Flexural areas"},{"letter":"C","text":"Palms"},{"letter":"D","text":"Scalp"}],"multi":null,"correctSet":[],"answerIdx":null,"answerLetter":null,"answerText":null,"explanation":null},{"n":66,"chapter":"Psychiatry","src":"Loksewa paper p. 6 (Medical Officer 2083-01-04)","pdfPage":6,"stem":"False perception without external stimulation is known as:","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"Illusion"},{"letter":"B","text":"Hallucination"},{"letter":"C","text":"Delusion"},{"letter":"D","text":"Obsession"}],"multi":null,"correctSet":[],"answerIdx":null,"answerLetter":null,"answerText":null,"explanation":null},{"n":67,"chapter":"Psychiatry","src":"Loksewa paper p. 6 (Medical Officer 2083-01-04)","pdfPage":6,"stem":"What is the most common presentation of depression?","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"Insomnia"},{"letter":"B","text":"Headache"},{"letter":"C","text":"Nonspecific pain abdomen"},{"letter":"D","text":"Body ache"}],"multi":null,"correctSet":[],"answerIdx":null,"answerLetter":null,"answerText":null,"explanation":null},{"n":68,"chapter":"Psychiatry","src":"Loksewa paper p. 6 (Medical Officer 2083-01-04)","pdfPage":6,"stem":"What is the primary therapeutic use of benzodiazepines?","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"Antidepressant effect"},{"letter":"B","text":"Mood stabilization"},{"letter":"C","text":"Anxiolytic and sedative effects"},{"letter":"D","text":"Antipsychotic effect"}],"multi":null,"correctSet":[],"answerIdx":null,"answerLetter":null,"answerText":null,"explanation":null},{"n":69,"chapter":"Psychiatry","src":"Loksewa paper p. 6 (Medical Officer 2083-01-04)","pdfPage":6,"stem":"A patient present in the ward, when asked \"What is your name?\" repeats the same sentence back to you. What is the phenomenon called?","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"Coprolalia"},{"letter":"B","text":"Echopraxia"},{"letter":"C","text":"Copropraxia"},{"letter":"D","text":"Echolalia"}],"multi":null,"correctSet":[],"answerIdx":null,"answerLetter":null,"answerText":null,"explanation":null},{"n":70,"chapter":"Psychiatry","src":"Loksewa paper p. 6 (Medical Officer 2083-01-04)","pdfPage":6,"stem":"Which one of the following is an organic brain disorder resulting from damage to the mamillary bodies, dorsomedial nuclei of the thalamus and adjacent areas of periventricular grey matter caused by a deficiency of thiamin (Vitamin B1)?","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"Wernicke-Korsakoff syndrome"},{"letter":"B","text":"Delirium"},{"letter":"C","text":"Mallory-Weiss syndrome"},{"letter":"D","text":"Wernicke's encephalopathy"}],"multi":null,"correctSet":[],"answerIdx":null,"answerLetter":null,"answerText":null,"explanation":null},{"n":71,"chapter":"Medicine","src":"Loksewa paper p. 6 (Medical Officer 2083-01-04)","pdfPage":6,"stem":"Which blood test is useful test of the presence of diabetes as it provides an average of blood glucose over several months?","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"Point of care finger prick"},{"letter":"B","text":"Venous blood sample"},{"letter":"C","text":"Venous HbA1C sample"},{"letter":"D","text":"Urine glucose dipstick sample"}],"multi":null,"correctSet":[],"answerIdx":null,"answerLetter":null,"answerText":null,"explanation":null},{"n":72,"chapter":"Anatomy","src":"Loksewa paper p. 6 (Medical Officer 2083-01-04)","pdfPage":6,"stem":"Which is the longest organ of digestive system in human body?","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"Pancreatic duct"},{"letter":"B","text":"Large intestine"},{"letter":"C","text":"Small intestine"},{"letter":"D","text":"Esophagus"}],"multi":null,"correctSet":[],"answerIdx":null,"answerLetter":null,"answerText":null,"explanation":null},{"n":73,"chapter":"Medicine","src":"Loksewa paper p. 6 (Medical Officer 2083-01-04)","pdfPage":6,"stem":"Pulmonary eosinophilia can be caused by all EXCEPT:","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"Ascaris"},{"letter":"B","text":"Nitrofurantoin"},{"letter":"C","text":"Plasmodium vivax"},{"letter":"D","text":"Aspergillus fumigatus"}],"multi":null,"correctSet":[],"answerIdx":null,"answerLetter":null,"answerText":null,"explanation":null},{"n":74,"chapter":"Medicine","src":"Loksewa paper p. 6 (Medical Officer 2083-01-04)","pdfPage":6,"stem":"Which subtype of the Influenza A virus is known for causing severe bird flu outbreaks in humans?","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"H1N1"},{"letter":"B","text":"H5N1"},{"letter":"C","text":"H3N2"},{"letter":"D","text":"H7N9"}],"multi":null,"correctSet":[],"answerIdx":null,"answerLetter":null,"answerText":null,"explanation":null},{"n":75,"chapter":"Surgery","src":"Loksewa paper p. 6 (Medical Officer 2083-01-04)","pdfPage":6,"stem":"Gastric cancer is strongly associated with which one of the following?","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"Alcohol"},{"letter":"B","text":"Smoking"},{"letter":"C","text":"H pylori"},{"letter":"D","text":"Aflatoxin in food"}],"multi":null,"correctSet":[],"answerIdx":null,"answerLetter":null,"answerText":null,"explanation":null},{"n":76,"chapter":"Neurology","src":"Loksewa paper p. 7 (Medical Officer 2083-01-04)","pdfPa